On any given real platform, there is a ceiling on your hit points
and on the capacity of your icebox.  This then gives rise to a
[insanely low] probability of starvation or combat death that does
not decrease with time.  All things being equal, this provides a
theoretical guarantee for your ultimate demise.  (The expected lifetime
of the universe may, however, provide a tighter bound on your
in-game survival).

